  "note": {
    "version": 1,
    "body": "# Planning the Copenhagen design conference\n\n**Date:** June 8\n**Attendees:** Nina Castellanos, Sam Kowalski\n\n## Summary\n\nPlanning session for the studio's attendance at the DesignOps Summit in Copenhagen, including the talk proposal, budget and travel.\n\n## The conference\n\n- Nina and Sam will attend the DesignOps Summit in Copenhagen from September 14 to September 16, on behalf of the studio. This is a work trip, paid from the studio's events budget.\n- The studio's talk proposal on the Harbourline onboarding research was accepted. Nina presents; Sam runs the live demo.\n- Booth space was considered and rejected: too expensive for a studio of our size.\n\n## Decisions\n\n- Brambleway will not take a booth at the summit this year and will put the money into the talk and a small client dinner instead.\n\n## Action items\n\n- **Sam Kowalski** — book flights and the hotel for the summit by June 19.\n- **Nina Castellanos** — send the final talk outline to the summit organisers.\n\n## Personal\n\n- Sam is staying on after the summit for a week of cycling through Denmark with Tessa, his wife, from September 17 to September 24. That part is personal leave, and he will book it separately from the studio travel.\n- Tessa is flying in on the last day of the summit to meet him.\n\n## Next steps\n\nWe rehearse the talk internally in the last week of August, and Nina confirms the client dinner guest list with Harbourline by the end of July.\n"
  },
